Objective:
Fix the layout of the Child List items on the Dashboard so the full name is visible. Currently, the "Log Hours" button is too wide and truncating the name to a single letter (e.g., "E...").

1. Adjust the Flex Container:

    In app/page.js (or the Dashboard component), find the list item row for each child.
    It is likely a flex container.
    Action: Give the name container flex-grow (or flex-1) so it takes up all available space.

2. Shrink the Button:

    The "Log Hours" button is likely too wide on mobile.
    Action:
        Remove any fixed width classes (like w-32 or w-1/2).
        Reduce the padding (e.g., px-3 instead of px-6).
        Mobile Optimization: On very small screens, hide the text "Log Hours" and just show the Clock Icon, OR change the text to just "Log".
        Example: <span className="hidden sm:inline">Log Hours</span><span className="sm:hidden">Log</span>

3. Text Truncation Settings:

    Check the class on the name text. It probably has truncate.
    Keep truncate, but ensure its parent container has min-w-0 (this is a Tailwind flexbox trick to allow truncation to work properly inside a flex child).

4. Layout Structure:

    Ensure the structure is: [Icon] [Name & Hours (Flex-Grow)] [Button (Flex-Shrink-0)]

Please adjust the CSS classes to ensure the full name "Emma" or "George" is visible.